        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: parse zero-argument XML tool calls",
        "body": "Closes #102933\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users running models that emit zero-parameter XML-ish tool calls such as `<function=get_system_info></function>` would have those calls rejected by tool-call-repair, so the call never promoted into an executable tool invocation and could leak into visible chat text instead.\n\nRelated open candidates: #102954, #102975. This PR keeps zero-argument acceptance limited to explicit `<function=...>` openings, preserves bracket rejection, and also covers the stream normalizer / end-offset path so streaming promotion does not treat `</function>` as impossible text.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe XML-ish parser and stream helpers required at least one `<parameter=...>` body. That is correct for bracketed openings that must not become empty tool calls, but too strict for explicit `<function=name></function>` forms that legitimately carry `{}` arguments.\n\nThe fix adds an opt-in `allowsZeroArguments` flag for XML function openings, accepts zero-parameter close tags in `findXmlishToolCallEnd`, and lets the stream buffer continue through a zero-argument `</function>` close.\n\n## User Impact\n\nModels that emit zero-argument XML-ish tool calls are now recognized and repaired instead of being dropped or shown as raw text. Bracket-only markers such as `[tool:name]` still do not become empty tool calls.\n\n## Evidence\n\nLocal focused tests (Blacksmith Testbox binary missing; AWS Crabbox broker not logged in on this machine):\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n    packages/tool-call-repair/src/grammar.test.ts \\\n    packages/tool-call-repair/src/stream-normalizer.test.ts \\\n    src/plugin-sdk/tool-payload.test.ts\n\n✓ |unit-fast| src/plugin-sdk/tool-payload.test.ts (27 tests)\n✓ |unit| packages/tool-call-repair/src/stream-normalizer.test.ts (2 tests)\n✓ |unit| packages/tool-call-repair/src/grammar.test.ts (4 tests)\n\nTest Files  passed across unit-fast + unit shards\n```\n\nCoverage added:\n\n- parse zero-argument `<function=...></function>` into `{ arguments: {} }`\n- strip zero-argument XML calls from visible text\n- keep bare bracket openings from becoming zero-argument calls\n- `findXmlishToolCallEnd` for zero-arg XML and bracket rejection\n- stream normalizer promotes zero-arg XML without leaking the text delta",
